  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Leaving a job",
     "texto": [
      "To leave a job voluntarily, use **уволиться** («to resign»). To say «leave work» in the sense of going away from the workplace, use **уйти с работы**: **Я ухожу с работы в пять** («I leave work at five»). **Увольнение** names the end of employment: it can be voluntary or a decision by the company, so it does not always mean «dismissal».",
      "**Перейти** («to move») takes **на**: **перейти на другую работу** («to move to another job»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "I was given and I was offered",
     "texto": [
      "With **дать** («to give») the person who receives goes in the dative: **Мне дали отпуск** («I was given holiday»). With **предложить** («to offer») it is the same: **Мне предложили новую работу** («I was offered a new job»).",
      "**Собираться** + infinitive expresses a plan or intention; it does not on its own mean that the action will happen immediately: **Я собираюсь уволиться** («I plan to resign»). The perfective **начать** forms the simple future **начну**: **я начну работать** («I will start working»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
